{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773073625,"nonce":"sguXdoAGgTDD0RcmDhLFqQ7aD2A=","title":"Repos tab: register new repo via file-open dialog or newproj-style creation","message":"Currently repos are discovered automatically at startup. There is no way from the UI to manually register a repo that was missed (e.g. too deep for the scan) or to create a new project.\n\n## Two desired entry points\n\n1. **Register existing repo**: file-open dialog (or path input) to locate an existing git repo and add it to the tracked set. Equivalent to the current workaround of adding it to repos.toml and restarting.\n\n2. **Create new project**: equivalent to the `newproj` skill in dotfiles — prompts for name, path, remote, creates the repo, registers it in repos.toml, and adds it to Mandible tracking. Could be a simple form in the Repos tab or a wizard panel.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `newproj` skill is at `~/.claude/skills/newproj.md` — its steps are a useful reference for what \"create new project\" entails\n- After registering, Mandible should scan the new repo immediately (no restart required)\n- The repos.toml fix (issue 7ed20d0) makes this more tractable: registering = writing a new entry to repos.toml + triggering a rescan","files":null}]}